{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"d4c5a7bc","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.007816,"end_time":"2026-11-18T16:39:48.334852+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-18T16:39:48.327036+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Asteroid Analysis"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"3dd62a51","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.006391,"end_time":"2026-11-18T16:39:48.347832+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-18T16:39:48.341441+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["In this project I explore an asteroid dataset to see how asteroids are spread across classes and how big they are. I started by cleaning the data: removing duplicates and columns I did not need, fixing data types and getting rid of values that are not possible. Some missing values could be filled using other columns, but I left diameter and albedo empty since most of them are missing. After that I looked at asteroid classes, NEOs, PHAs, diameter and how diameter relates to absolute magnitude (H)."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"124efa35","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.006125,"end_time":"2026-11-18T16:39:48.360333+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-18T16:39:48.354208+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**Loading and Cleaning the Data**"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"ea7364e4","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T16:39:48.376036Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T16:39:48.375686Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.58117Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.580037Z"},"papermill":{"duration":72.215775,"end_time":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.583395+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-18T16:39:48.36762+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Shape: (958524, 45)\n","id                 object\n","spkid               int64\n","full_name          object\n","pdes               object\n","name               object\n","prefix             object\n","neo                object\n","pha                object\n","H                 float64\n","diameter          float64\n","albedo            float64\n","diameter_sigma    float64\n","orbit_id           object\n","epoch             float64\n","epoch_mjd           int64\n","epoch_cal         float64\n","equinox            object\n","e                 float64\n","a                 float64\n","q                 float64\n","i                 float64\n","om                float64\n","w                 float64\n","ma                float64\n","ad                float64\n","n                 float64\n","tp                float64\n","tp_cal            float64\n","per               float64\n","per_y             float64\n","moid              float64\n","moid_ld           float64\n","sigma_e           float64\n","sigma_a           float64\n","sigma_q           float64\n","sigma_i           float64\n","sigma_om          float64\n","sigma_w           float64\n","sigma_ma          float64\n","sigma_ad          float64\n","sigma_n           float64\n","sigma_tp          float64\n","sigma_per         float64\n","class              object\n","rms               float64\n","dtype: object\n","\n","Missing values:\n","name              936460\n","prefix            958506\n","neo                    4\n","pha                19921\n","H                   6263\n","diameter          822315\n","albedo            823421\n","diameter_sigma    822443\n","ma                     1\n","ad                     4\n","per                    4\n","per_y                  1\n","moid               19921\n","moid_ld              127\n","sigma_e            19922\n","sigma_a            19922\n","sigma_q            19922\n","sigma_i            19922\n","sigma_om           19922\n","sigma_w            19922\n","sigma_ma           19922\n","sigma_ad           19926\n","sigma_n            19922\n","sigma_tp           19922\n","sigma_per          19926\n","rms                    2\n","dtype: int64\n","\n","Equinox values: ['J2000']\n","\n","Duplicate rows: 0\n","Rows with e outside 0 to 1: 4\n","PHA rule matches known labels: 0.9999\n","\n","Missing values after cleaning:\n","diameter           822311\n","albedo             823417\n","diameter_sigma     822439\n","ma                      1\n","moid                  127\n","moid_ld               127\n","sigma_e             19922\n","sigma_a             19922\n","sigma_q             19922\n","sigma_i             19922\n","sigma_om            19922\n","sigma_w             19922\n","sigma_ma            19922\n","sigma_ad            19922\n","sigma_n             19922\n","sigma_tp            19922\n","sigma_per           19922\n","rms                     2\n","perihelion_date         1\n","dtype: int64\n","\n","Shape after cleaning: (958520, 45)\n","Asteroids with a measured diameter: 136209\n"]}],"source":["import pandas as pd\n","import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","\n","df = pd.read_csv(\"/kaggle/input/datasets/manishamali/asteroid-dataset-analysis/dataset.csv\", low_memory=False)\n","\n","print(\"Shape:\", df.shape)\n","print(df.dtypes)\n","print(\"\\nMissing values:\")\n","print(df.isnull().sum()[df.isnull().sum() > 0])\n","\n","# prefix is almost empty and equinox is J2000 for every asteroid\n","print(\"\\nEquinox values:\", df[\"equinox\"].unique())\n","df = df.drop(columns=[\"prefix\", \"equinox\"])\n","\n","text_cols = [\"id\", \"full_name\", \"pdes\", \"name\", \"neo\", \"pha\", \"orbit_id\", \"class\"]\n","for col in text_cols:\n","    df[col] = df[col].astype(\"string\").str.strip()\n","\n","print(\"\\nDuplicate rows:\", df.duplicated().sum())\n","df = df.drop_duplicates()\n","\n","num_cols = [c for c in df.columns if c not in text_cols]\n","df[num_cols] = df[num_cols].apply(pd.to_numeric, errors=\"coerce\")\n","\n","# epoch_cal and tp_cal are stored like 20200531.5\n","df[\"epoch_date\"] = pd.to_datetime(df[\"epoch_cal\"].astype(int).astype(str), format=\"%Y%m%d\", errors=\"coerce\")\n","df[\"perihelion_date\"] = pd.to_datetime(df[\"tp_cal\"].astype(int).astype(str), format=\"%Y%m%d\", errors=\"coerce\")\n","\n","# values that are not possible\n","df.loc[df[\"diameter\"] <= 0, \"diameter\"] = np.nan\n","df.loc[~df[\"albedo\"].between(0, 1), \"albedo\"] = np.nan\n","df.loc[~df[\"i\"].between(0, 180), \"i\"] = np.nan\n","for col in [\"q\", \"per\", \"per_y\", \"moid\", \"moid_ld\", \"rms\"]:\n","    df.loc[df[col] < 0, col] = np.nan\n","\n","# angles above 360 just need to wrap around\n","for col in [\"om\", \"w\", \"ma\"]:\n","    df[col] = df[col] % 360\n","\n","# e >= 1 is a hyperbolic orbit so these are not normal asteroids\n","print(\"Rows with e outside 0 to 1:\", ((df[\"e\"] < 0) | (df[\"e\"] >= 1)).sum())\n","df = df[(df[\"e\"] >= 0) & (df[\"e\"] < 1)].copy()\n","\n","# moid_ld is the same distance in lunar distances (1 au = 389.17 LD)\n","df[\"moid\"] = df[\"moid\"].fillna(df[\"moid_ld\"] / 389.17)\n","\n","# a PHA is a NEO with moid <= 0.05 au and H <= 22\n","pha_rule = np.where((df[\"neo\"] == \"Y\") & (df[\"moid\"] <= 0.05) & (df[\"H\"] <= 22), \"Y\", \"N\")\n","known = df[\"pha\"].notna()\n","match = (pha_rule[known] == df.loc[known, \"pha\"]).mean()\n","print(\"PHA rule matches known labels:\", round(match, 4))\n","\n","missing = df[\"pha\"].isna() & df[\"moid\"].notna() & df[\"H\"].notna()\n","df.loc[missing, \"pha\"] = pha_rule[missing]\n","df[\"pha\"] = df[\"pha\"].fillna(\"Unknown\")\n","\n","df[\"H\"] = df[\"H\"].fillna(df.groupby(\"class\")[\"H\"].transform(\"median\"))\n","\n","# not filling diameter and albedo, around 86% of them are missing\n","df[\"name\"] = df[\"name\"].fillna(\"Unnamed\")\n","df[\"orbit_id\"] = df[\"orbit_id\"].fillna(\"Unknown\")\n","\n","for col in [\"neo\", \"pha\", \"class\"]:\n","    df[col] = df[col].astype(\"category\")\n","\n","print(\"\\nMissing values after cleaning:\")\n","print(df.isnull().sum()[df.isnull().sum() > 0])\n","print(\"\\nShape after cleaning:\", df.shape)\n","print(\"Asteroids with a measured diameter:\", df[\"diameter\"].notna().sum())\n","\n","df.to_csv(\"/kaggle/working/asteroid_cleaned.csv\", index=False)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"2528c6ec","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.006687,"end_time":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.597007+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.59032+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["*There were no duplicate rows. I dropped prefix because it is almost empty, and equinox because it is J2000 for every row. 4 asteroids had e >= 1 (hyperbolic orbits), so I removed them. Missing moid values were filled from moid_ld, and missing PHA labels were filled using the PHA rule (NEO, moid <= 0.05 au and H <= 22) after checking that it matched 99.99% of the known labels. H was filled with the median of each class. Diameter and albedo are missing for about 86% of rows, so I did not fill them. That leaves 136,209 asteroids with a real diameter.*"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"af46a013","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.006712,"end_time":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.611041+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.604329+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**Number of asteroids in each class**"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"52647f0e","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.626782Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.62603Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.640578Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.639569Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.02468,"end_time":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.642562+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.617882+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Number of asteroids in each class:\n","class\n","MBA    855954\n","OMB     28355\n","IMB     20360\n","MCA     18685\n","APO     12687\n","AMO      8457\n","TJN      8221\n","TNO      3468\n","ATE      1729\n","CEN       506\n","AST        76\n","IEO        22\n","Name: count, dtype: int64\n"]}],"source":["# Number of asteroids in each class\n","class_count = df[\"class\"].value_counts()\n","\n","print(\"Number of asteroids in each class:\")\n","print(class_count)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"996e1290","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.006742,"end_time":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.656274+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.649532+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["*MBA is by far the biggest class with 855,954 asteroids. IEO is the smallest with only 22.*"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"02d2430f","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.006551,"end_time":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.669743+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.663192+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**Number of Near Earth Objects (NEOs)**"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"id":"41a51de3","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.684929Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.684573Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.700355Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.699314Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.025868,"end_time":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.702481+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.676613+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["NEO classification:\n","neo\n","N    935625\n","Y     22895\n","Name: count, dtype: int64\n","Total NEOs: 22895\n"]}],"source":["# Number of Near Earth Objects (NEOs)\n","neo_count = df[\"neo\"].value_counts()\n","\n","print(\"NEO classification:\")\n","print(neo_count)\n","\n","print(\"Total NEOs:\", neo_count[\"Y\"])"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"9b7c9415","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.00698,"end_time":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.716946+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-18T16:41:00.709966+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["*Only 22,895 asteroids are NEOs, which is arou